{"Docs":[{"DocType":1,"IsAmended":false,"IsUpdated":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocOrderId":7,"AmendedBy":[],"Notes":[],"Drafts":[],"ChunkGroupStartingNodeId":"PTICHCO_TIT1IN","NodeDepth":2,"TitleHtml":"<div class=\"chunk-title\">Sec. 1.2. - City to have perpetual existence.</div>","ShouldShowMiniToc":false,"Id":"PTICHCO_TIT1IN_S1.2CIHAPEEX","Title":"Sec. 1.2. - City to have perpetual existence.","Content":"<div class=\"chunk-content\">\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               The City of Chattanooga, Tennessee, as a municipal corporation and body politic, shall\n               have perpetual existence, and shall be considered for all purposes to have had perpetual\n               existence since being first chartered by the General Assembly; and no act of said\n               city, including the issuance of bonds, shall be affected in any manner by any prior\n               charter provision to the contrary that may not have been expressly amended or repealed\n               heretofore.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"historynote0\">\n               (Priv. Acts 1969, Ch. 82, § 4)\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refeditor0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>Editor's note— </b>\n               Part I of this Volume contains the compilation of the Acts of the Tennessee General\n               Assembly and Home Rule amendments adopted by the voters of the City pursuant to Art.\n               11, § 9 of the Constitution of Tennessee. Historically, the Charter has been arranged\n               according to subject matter and each provision assigned an arbitrary section number\n               to facilitate referencing and indexing. Although major changes to the Charter were\n               made prior to the 2013 publication of the Charter, the historic numbering system has\n               been maintained to the extent practicable to facilitate cross-referencing and legal\n               research.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refmanual0\" block_type=\"hang\">\n               The adoption of Home Rule was submitted to the voters to ratify Ordinance No. 6489,\n               9-19-72 pursuant to Art. 11, § 9 of the Constitution of Tennessee on November 7, 1972,\n               and approved by a vote of 15,895 to 8,190. A list of Home Rule ordinances that have\n               been duly ratified by the voters pursuant to Art. 11, § 9 set forth below. All amendments\n               have been worked into their proper places and amended or repealed revisions deleted.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refmanual0\" block_type=\"hang\">\n               Legislation that has clearly been superseded by subsequent legislation has been deleted.\n               This provision is set out in the language in which it was enacted, but the editors\n               have added clarifying words or phrases in brackets where necessary. The bracketed\n               material should not, of course, be considered authoritative, but is for convenience\n               and clarity only.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refmanual0\" block_type=\"hang\">\n               Ordinance No. 11272, 5-2-02, approved by referendum amended and restated the Charter\n               of the City in its entirety so as to conform to the decision of the United States\n               District Court in <span class=\"ital\">Brown v. Board of Commissioners</span>, U.S.D.C. No. CIV-1-87-388 and subsequent amendments thereto. The Court of Appeals\n               of Tennessee held in the case of <span class=\"ital\">Ron Littlefield v. Hamilton County Election Commission, et al</span>, No. 11C1520, that Ordinance No. 11272, was \"<span class=\"ital\">sufficient to 'enact' a 'contrary charter provision'</span> pursuant to Tennessee Code Annotated Section 2-5-151 (i)...\" (page 17 of opinion).\n               The editors are of the opinion that based upon this Court of Appeals decision that\n               Ordinance No. 11272 is the baseline for the present charter.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refmanual0\" block_type=\"hang\">\n               Michael A. McMahan, City Attorney, 2009-2013, is the principal editor of this 2013\n               publication of the Charter of the City of Chattanooga. Thanks is given to Maria Sirchia\n               for her ongoing efforts to accurately maintain the Charter and City Code.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               The following Home Rule Ordinances approved by referendum have been compiled in this\n               Charter of the City of Chattanooga:\n               \n               <div>\n                  <div class=\"\" style=\"width:100%\">\n                     <table class=\"thead0 table  left\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"1\" rules=\"all\" style=\"font-size:11px;\">\n                        <colgroup class=\"std\">\n                           <col width=\"33.333333333333336%\">\n                           <col width=\"33.333333333333336%\">\n                           <col width=\"33.333333333333336%\">\n                        </colgroup>\n                        <tbody>\n                           <tr>\n                              <td class=\" top \">\n                                 <span class=\"bold\">\n                                    <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"TIT2COPOPRGE\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"15385\">TITLE 2</a>\n                                    </span>\n                                 </td>\n                              <td class=\" top \">\n                                 <span class=\"bold\">ORDINANCE NO.</span>\n                                 </td>\n                              <td class=\" top \">\n                                 <span class=\"bold\">EFFECTIVE DATE</span>\n                                 </td>\n                           </tr>\n                           <tr>\n                              <td class=\" top \"></td>\n          